FAIL level_design: level-design review 6.5/10 (bar 8), 0 level(s) below 6/10:  Curve: The set is well structured: 10 chapters, each introducing one mechanic (void, stamp, color-cross, smudged, cracked, chain), with a teach, practise, boss, breather, twist and masterwork cadence, and difficulty rises from about 100% casual wins to the mid-50s to 60s. The weaknesses are these. (1) Teach levels 1-3 have a flat ramp. L1 and L2 are 100% wins with almost no insight. (2) Chapter 2 (L13-L24) is "reach" with many near-identical animal silhouettes. L14, L15, L16, L17 and L21 are all "solid mass of overlap plus a few reaches", and the reach idea is rarely isolated. (3) Chapter 3 (colour, L25-L36) reuses the same "exact-fit with touching colours" insight in almost every level (L25, 26, 27, 29, 31, 32, 33, 35, 36), so there is little progression. (4) Breathers are not reliably easier than their neighbours. L7 (92%) and L19 (93%) are fine, but L31 (93%) follows an easy-ish L30 and sits next to a 79% boss. (5) The late levels fall off the targets in one direction. The last third averages about 60% casual, which is on target. But L82 (57%), L84 (55%) and L95 (55%) are the casual-win lows for their chapters, and L108 skilled is 86%. (6) Several cracked and smudged levels (L85-L96) state the "?" length as deducible but give a fairly mechanical bound. The 3-colour chapter (Conservatory) is the best at being non-obvious. (7) Chapter 10 pairs mechanics well (void+smudged, stamp+cracked), but L115 is a 90% breather inside a 53-65% run, which is correct placement. (8) Some doc claims about the boards are weak. L2's "13 optimal moves" is a pure exact-fit chain with no real choice.", "levels": [{"n":1,"rating":6,"problem":"Pure fill/X teach; easy-to-spot full 6s. No aha, though acceptable as an opener.","fix":"Keep, but make the handle and cup need one X-inference so the teach includes the X mark.","purpose":"teach fill+X"},{"n":2,"rating":6,"problem":"Exact-fit teach is clear but 100% win; mild.","fix":"Fine as is; consider trimming the one-cell mast artifact.","purpose":"teach exact fit"},{"n":3,"rating":7,"problem":"Overlap is a good third idea; the board is a fine jellyfish.","fix":"None needed.","purpose":"teach overlap"},{"n":4,"rating":7,"problem":"Gull and beam are asymmetric clutter in the top rows, but the lighthouse reads well.","fix":"Remove the gull to cut visual noise or merge it into the beam.","purpose":"practise exact-fit+overlap"},{"n":5,"rating":6,"problem":"Lopsided starfish is a shape with no strong idea; the eye X is a minor aha.","fix":"Make the eye a bigger visible hole so the X-deduction is the aha.","purpose":"practise overlap"},{"n":6,"rating":7,"problem":"A boss at 83% casual is a little soft, but the crab is memorable.","fix":"Add one more chained deduction so the boss feels tougher.","purpose":"boss"},{"n":7,"rating":7,"problem":"Fine breather; the umbrella is easy but similar in structure to L4.","fix":"None.","purpose":"breather"},{"n":8,"rating":7,"problem":"Split-clue overlap is a real twist; the board is a bit symmetric.","fix":"None.","purpose":"twist split clues"},{"n":9,"rating":6,"problem":"Anchor repeats the 'lone 1 walls row' idea with L2/L4; third consecutive near-identical practise.","fix":"Replace with a board that uses a different silhouette and an end-anchored clue.","purpose":"practise"},{"n":10,"rating":8,"problem":"","fix":"","purpose":"combine"},{"n":11,"rating":6,"problem":"The castle and the parasol are two unrelated mini-pictures sharing a board; the picture is hard to read.","fix":"Redraw as a single object, or shift the parasol closer to the castle.","purpose":"twist"},{"n":12,"rating":8,"problem":"","fix":"","purpose":"masterwork"},{"n":13,"rating":7,"problem":"Reach is the teach, but it overlaps visually with L1.","fix":"None.","purpose":"teach reach"},{"n":14,"rating":6,"problem":"Fox face is a second teach that restates the first and the stated reach is not clearly needed.","fix":"Remove most 